DESCRIPTION:National Whiskey Sour Day is observed on August 25 across the 
 United States. A whiskey sour is a classic cocktail containing whiskey (of
 ten bourbon)\, lemon juice\, and sugar. The oldest written recipe appears 
 in Jerry Thomas's The Bartender's Guide\, published in 1862.\n\nhttps://na
 tionaltoday.com/national-whiskey-sour-day/
LOCATION:Pastafarian Holy Day
URL:https://www.pastafariancalendar.com/whiskey-sour-day-2024-08-25?utm_so
