DESCRIPTION:Saturnalia was a Roman festival honoring Saturn\, god of seed 
 and sowing\, celebrated around the winter solstice. Originally on December
  17\, it lasted up to seven days (December 17-23). The most popular holida
 y of the Roman year\, it featured gift-giving\, feasting\, and role revers
 als.\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturnalia
