DESCRIPTION:Groundhog Day is a popular North American tradition observed i
 n the United States and Canada on February 2. It derives from the Pennsylv
 ania Dutch superstition that if a groundhog emerges from its burrow on thi
 s day and sees its shadow due to clear weather\, it will retreat to its de
 n\, and winter will go on for six more weeks\; if it does not see its shad
 ow because of cloudiness\, spring will arrive early.\n\nhttps://en.wikiped
 ia.org/wiki/Groundhog_Day
LOCATION:Pastafarian Holy Day
URL:https://www.pastafariancalendar.com/groundhog-day-2026-02-02?utm_sourc
