DESCRIPTION:Hogmanay is the Scots word for the last day of the old year an
 d is synonymous with the celebration of the New Year in the Scottish manne
 r. It is normally followed by further celebration on the morning of New Ye
 ar's Day (1 January) and\, in some cases\, 2 January (a Scottish bank holi
 day)\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hogmanay
